Description: Fix cookie_util.cc iterator type mismatch for system libc++
 In system libc++, std::string_view::begin() returns const char* while
 std::string::const_iterator is __wrap_iter<const char*>. These types are
 not implicitly convertible, causing compilation errors. Use auto to let
 the compiler deduce the correct iterator type from header_value.begin().
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <vejeta@gmail.com>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/915400
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-12-12

diff --git a/net/cookies/cookie_util.cc b/net/cookies/cookie_util.cc
index 79c7e45..a69383d 100644
--- a/net/cookies/cookie_util.cc
+++ b/net/cookies/cookie_util.cc
@@ -841,7 +841,7 @@ bool IsCookiePartitionedValid(const GURL& url,

